# Add Simple Readline Loop

## Goal Description
Implement a simple Read-Eval-Print Loop (REPL) in [Program.cs](file:///c:/Users/jenar/MyFirstProject/Program.cs) that reads user input and echoes it back until the user types "exit".

## Proposed Changes

### MyFirstProject

#### [MODIFY] [Program.cs](file:///c:/Users/jenar/MyFirstProject/Program.cs)
- Replace the "Hello, World!" print with a `while` loop.
- Use `Console.ReadLine()` to get input.
- Print the input back to the console.
- Break the loop if input is "exit".

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Run the application using `dotnet run`.
- Type various strings to see them echoed.
- Type "exit" to verify the application terminates.
